      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order verified; late-event determination incomplete\n\nThe relevant Racine manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work-order ID **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack**.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable from the supplied records |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event record |\n\nThe supporting transaction input returns **404: “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** The available source contains work-order and cost-period records, but no cost-event rows. Consequently, I cannot establish whether an event was created after Pending Close. **This is not a finding that no late event occurred.** The timestamp above is reproduced exactly as stored; no time-zone offset is supplied.\n\n### Oracle Pending Close treatment\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* documentation states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period **will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to process, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions and continue processing.**\n\nThus, an ordinary, non-exempt transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held while September remains Pending Close. The actual event’s compliance cannot be assessed without its creation time, type, and recorded accounting status.\n\n**Sources:** supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records; Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B policy excerpt, PDF page 233, printed page 225.\n\nNo database records were changed. The incomplete audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_59f494765143/audit-report.json`; the submitted report is marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
